package term

import str

// SGR: colours and text attributes, plus the escape-aware string helpers
// (Strip, Width, PadRight, Truncate) that ordinary str/fmt functions get
// wrong the moment a string contains an escape sequence.
//
// Every colouring function is gated on SupportsColor(), so the SAME code
// prints colour on a terminal and clean text into a pipe or a log file.
// Reach for the `Seq*` functions when you want the raw sequence regardless.
//
// Nesting composes correctly: Paint rewrites any reset already inside the
// text so that an inner colour hands control back to the outer one instead
// of cancelling it, which is what makes Bold(Red("x") + " y") come out with
// " y" still bold.
//
// WIDTH IS COUNTED IN CODEPOINTS. Width/PadRight/Truncate ignore escape
// sequences (that is their whole point) but do not implement East-Asian
// wide-character or combining-mark rules, so a CJK or emoji column will be
// narrower on screen than the count suggests.

// ------------------------------------------------------------------ codes

@en "Reset"
@fa "بازنشانی"
@ar "إعادة ضبط"
pub const Reset := "\x1b[0m"

@en "StyleBold"
@fa "سبک ضخیم"
@ar "نمط عریض"
pub const StyleBold := 1

